title: About
---
eyebrow: THE PERSON BEHIND THE WORK
---
summary: A physicist working across science, software, and technical leadership.
---
body:

My work spans scientific computing, statistical modeling, data science, machine learning, and software development.

I began with physics and biomedical research, where precise questions and reproducible answers matter. That analytical foundation continues to shape how I build software today: start by understanding the problem, make assumptions explicit, and build systems that people can trust.

I currently lead software platform development, including architecture, backend engineering, code reviews, and technical decisions. I'm particularly interested in research and development environments where scientific depth and practical engineering reinforce each other.
